I take your point. If "sekaileka" were English, we'd end up pronouncing
it "skalka", nice and short, but we can't do that in Lojban, which is
why I feel Lojban needs to create some sort of compensatory alternative.
I already know that the consensus is against this, so there is no
need for another wave of disagreeing replies.

