The one and only thing that makes Lojban superior to other engineered
languages is the one and only thing that makes Esperanto superior to
other IALs: the community (not just of outright users, but also of
participants, collaborators, etc.). Even at this stage, but with the
benefit of lessons learnt from Lojban, several of us could redesign
Lojban and come up with something vastly better. And perhaps some of
us do do this, privately. But while it may be within our individual
powers to design a better language, it is not within our individual
powers to create a community around it. And certainly not a
community of the calibre of Lojban's.

